<div style="background-color: #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; color: white; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: 2em;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Let's Dress for a Dance. – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.2em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> Our Traditional Style of Dress</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> Let's Dress for a Dance.</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Clarify oral questions in group activities.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can pick out details about time, quantities, and location in talks about clothing (e.g., 'Women wear this dress at festivals.').
            Can respond to and clarify oral questions, in group activities, about traditional clothing (e.g., 'What is she wearing?' 'She is wearing a dress.').
            Can ask and answer questions about where and when clothing is worn (e.g., 'Where do people wear this?' 'At festivals.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 10px; text-align: left; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows flashcards of different traditional Panamanian clothing (e.g., pollera, montuno, cutarras). Students point and say "Yes!" if they recognize it or "No" if not. The teacher says "Look! This is beautiful attire." and points to a pollera. "We wear this for a special event." The teacher connects it to the theme "Let's Dress for a Dance." by showing a picture of people dancing in traditional clothing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher presents new vocabulary words: 'attire', 'celebration', 'event', 'traditional clothing', 'jewelry', 'wear', 'festive', 'beautiful'. The teacher models clear pronunciation, especially the /w/ sound in 'wearing' and the /t/ sound in 'traditional', and the blend /dr/ /ɛs/ for 'dress' and /pr-ɪ-t-i/ for 'pretty'. Students listen and repeat chorally and individually. The teacher points to clothing items and says, "She is wearing a beautiful dress."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Pointing to a picture of everyday clothes) "Is this traditional clothing?" (Expected answer: No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(Pointing to a picture of a pollera) "Do we wear this for a celebration or for school?" (Expected answer: For a celebration)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio dialogue (or teacher-read dialogue) between two friends, Ana and Luis, talking about what people are wearing at a local traditional dance festival. The dialogue is simple and uses the target vocabulary and grammar structures (Present continuous, WH-questions, Present simple). For example: "Luis: Look, Ana! What is she wearing? Ana: She is wearing a beautiful pollera. People wear this traditional attire at festivals. Luis: And what about him? Ana: He is wearing a montuno. It's for the celebration."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Understanding spoken descriptions of traditional clothing and its use in cultural events.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks (Listening):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> The teacher asks, "What are Ana and Luis talking about?" (Expected answer: Traditional clothing / A festival). Students listen to the dialogue once.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> Students listen to the dialogue again and answer True or False to statements like: "The girl is wearing a modern dress." (False) "People wear polleras at festivals." (True).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information Matching:</b> The teacher writes names of clothing (pollera, montuno) and occasions (festival, dance) on the board. Students listen and match the clothing to when it is worn.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>10-12 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Present continuous (e.g., 'She is wearing...'), WH-questions (e.g., 'What are you wearing?'), Present simple (e.g., 'Women wear this dress at festivals.').</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> attire, celebration, event, traditional clothing, jewelry, wear, festive, beautiful, cultural, important.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Describing traditional clothing: 'She is wearing a pollera.'</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> /w/ in 'wearing', /t/ in 'traditional', /dr/ /ɛs/ in 'dress', /pr-ɪ-t-i/ in 'pretty'.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice – Listen & Fill-in-the-Blanks:</b> The teacher reads sentences aloud related to traditional clothing with missing words (e.g., "She is _______ a beautiful _______. They wear it at a _______."). Students listen and write the missing vocabulary words (wearing, attire/dress, celebration/event) on their worksheet. The teacher repeats each sentence twice.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-Controlled Practice – Listen & Choose:</b> The teacher presents three pictures of different traditional clothing items (A, B, C). The teacher then describes one picture orally, e.g., "This is a festive dress. It has a lot of colorful jewelry." Students listen and circle the correct picture (A, B, or C). Repeat with several descriptions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction – Listen & Clarify:</b> Students work in pairs. Each pair receives a card with a simple drawing of someone wearing a traditional clothing item (e.g., a girl in a pollera). Partner A describes their drawing to Partner B, but intentionally omits a key detail or uses a slightly unclear word (e.g., "She is wearing a beautiful... thing on her head."). Partner B must listen carefully and ask a clarifying WH-question: "What is she wearing on her head?" or "What kind of clothing is it?" Partner A then clarifies. They switch roles.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>15-18 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Our Traditional Style of Dress"</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion and Collaborative Description.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group is given a picture of a Panamanian dance scene (e.g., a "tamborito" or "punta") but the people in the picture are only outlines – they are not wearing any specific traditional clothing. The teacher explains that they need to "dress" the people for the dance by deciding what each person is wearing based on what they learned. Students engage in a group discussion, listening to each other's ideas and clarifying questions to decide on the attire.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Instructions:</b> "Imagine you are dressing these dancers for a big celebration. Listen to your friends. What is he/she wearing? Where do people wear this? If you don't understand, ask 'What did you say?' or 'Can you explain?' Talk together and decide what each dancer is wearing."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students must use the target vocabulary (traditional clothing, festive, beautiful, wear, attire, jewelry, event, celebration) and grammar (Present continuous, WH-questions, Present simple) to describe and agree. The primary focus is on active listening and clarifying any oral questions during the group interaction.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>8-10 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> The teacher circulates among the groups during the production stage, observing and noting students' ability to listen, ask clarifying questions, and use target vocabulary and grammar when describing traditional clothing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Listening Focus):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Student clarifies oral questions from peers (e.g., "What did you say?", "Can you repeat?").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Student responds to oral questions about traditional clothing appropriately.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. Student uses target vocabulary (e.g., 'traditional clothing', 'festive', 'wear') when listening and responding.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">4. Student demonstrates comprehension of descriptions (e.g., points to correct clothing item).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a short paper strip (exit ticket) before leaving.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What new word about clothing did you hear today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "Draw what someone is wearing for a dance based on your friend's description." (Teacher gives a very brief oral description for students to listen to and draw, e.g., "She is wearing a beautiful dress and jewelry for the celebration.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>5-7 min</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; color: #1a5276;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompts:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. "What was easy for you to listen to today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. "What was difficult to understand when your friends spoke?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> Most students were able to identify key vocabulary and understand simple descriptions. Clarifying oral questions was more challenging for some, indicating a need for more explicit practice. The pronunciation of /w/ and /t/ sounds was grasped, and the blend in 'dress' and 'pretty' also showed good progress with modeling. I need to scaffold more opportunities for students to actively practice asking "What did you say?" or "Can you repeat?" in the next listening activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will read a short text about traditional clothing, using the vocabulary introduced today, to practice reading comprehension and reinforce the new words in context.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">__/__ - __/__<br>2-3 min</p></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>